Licensing Considerations
Purpose
This project requires Microsoft Entra ID and Microsoft 365 capabilities to support user onboarding, authentication, authorization, and access management.

Licensing Requirements
The following services were required for the implementation:

Microsoft Entra ID
Microsoft 365 administrative portal access
Microsoft Teams
SharePoint Online
OneDrive for Business
Exchange Online
Conditional Access (where available)
Group-based licensing (where supported)
Licence Assignment Strategy
To support scalability and simplify administration, licences were assigned through security groups rather than directly to individual users.

Example:

Group	Purpose
SG-LIC-M365-E5-SOC	Microsoft 365 licence assignment
This approach reduces administrative effort and simplifies future onboarding and offboarding activities.

Conditional Access Considerations
Conditional Access functionality depends on the licence available within the lab tenant.

Where Conditional Access was available:

MFA was required for targeted users.
Policies were initially deployed in Report-only mode.
Emergency access accounts were excluded from targeting.
Lab Limitations
The available functionality depended on the licences assigned to the lab tenant.

Any unavailable features were documented rather than simulated.

Examples may include:

Privileged Identity Management (PIM)
Identity Governance
Advanced Conditional Access features
Microsoft Defender integration
Security Considerations
Licensing decisions were aligned with least-privilege principles.

Users received only the services required for their role and no unnecessary administrative permissions were assigned.
